<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.WebAssembly">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
        <RootNamespace>AvCharts.Demo.Browser</RootNamespace>
        <AssemblyName>AvChartsDemoBrowser</AssemblyName>
        <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
        <!--
            Trimmed, and the reason is the download rather than the frame rate: measured, the published gallery
            goes from 70.7MB in 639 files to 35.7MB in 171, and every one of those megabytes is fetched before
            the page can draw (GitHub Pages does not compress the wasm, so the browser sees the sizes, not the
            brotli ones). What the trimmer must not touch is the XAML: the theme is loaded by URI at runtime
            (`ChartTheme.Create`, and the gallery's own `StyleInclude`), nothing references it from code, and
            the trimmer cannot tell it is wanted - measured: without the roots below the gallery comes up blank
            with `No precompiled XAML found for avares://AvCharts.Controls/Themes/ChartTheme.axaml`.

            Trimming is also the door to AOT, which the SDK refuses without it ("AOT is not supported without IL
            trimming"). AOT does now publish and run (`-p:RunAOTCompilation=true`), but it was measured *not* to
            change what a reader feels - the same pointer sweep and the same live page, before and after - while
            doubling the download to 73MB. So it stays a flag rather than a default; the jank that is left is
            the gallery re-reading and rebuilding a whole window of readings per frame, which is ours to fix in
            the series rather than the runtime's.

            The analysis warnings are quiet rather than off - `IL2026` and its neighbours are exactly what the
            roots answer, and rooting is what the trimmer's own advice would be here.
        -->
        <PublishTrimmed>true</PublishTrimmed>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);IL2026;IL2104;IL3050;IL3053</NoWarn>
        <!-- Same trade-off as the gallery: CS1591 is the libraries' rule, and a browser head is not API. -->
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Browser" />
        <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Fonts.Inter" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\AvCharts.Demo\AvCharts.Demo.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <!--
            The XAML-bearing assemblies, kept whole: see the note above `PublishTrimmed`. The libraries are
            rooted rather than a list of files, because the trimmer's unit is the assembly and their XAML is
            reached by URI rather than by name.
        -->
        <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="AvCharts" />
        <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="AvCharts.Controls" />
        <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="AvChartsDemo" />
        <TrimmerRootAssembly Include="iPaas.Controls" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
